          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "For a bounded set $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ and $R>0$, define its two-sided boundary layer\n$$\\partial_R\\Omega=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\operatorname{dist}(x,\\partial\\Omega)\\leq R\\},$$\nwhere distance is Euclidean distance and $|\\cdot|$ denotes $d$-dimensional Lebesgue measure. Boundary zero: The Definition fixes its parameter domain; no zero-limit result is proved here.",
