      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Use the cube $\\Lambda_L=[0,L)^d$ and the translation $T_x$ defined in [[def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference]]. Boundary empty: This definition requires positive-volume input and states no empty-object theorem.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Definition",
            "source_excerpt": "Use the cube $\\Lambda_L=[0,L)^d$ and the translation $T_x$ defined in [[def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference]]. For a finite configuration $\\omega\\subset\\Lambda_L$, let $\\omega^{(L)}=\\{q+Lk:q\\in\\omega,\\ k\\in\\mathbb Z^d\\}$ be its periodic continuation. Define its **periodized empirical field**\n$$R_{L,\\omega}:=\\frac1{L^d}\\int_{\\Lambda_L}\\delta_{T_x\\omega^{(L)}}\\,dx.$$\nThe integral is the push-forward of normalized Lebesgue measure on $\\Lambda_L$ under $x\\mapsto T_x\\omega^{(L)}$. For a probability law $C_L$ on finite configurations in $\\Lambda_L$, define its **empirical-field barycenter** $\\bar C_L$ by\n$$\\bar C_L(f):=\\int C_L(d\\omega)\\,R_{L,\\omega}(f)=\\frac1{L^d}\\int_{\\Lambda_L}E_{C_L}[f(T_x\\omega^{(L)})]\\,dx$$\nfor local tame $f$ from [[def-tdmath-local-tame-topology]]. This is a spatial average over the finite box, not the raw finite-volume law viewed at a fixed origin.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "4ea122d15e7dd7ba749c9128b87be5c42c860e261047579f05d29e051074e4af",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
