    "lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "It is lower regular if a nonnegative nonincreasing $\\psi:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,+\\infty]$ satisfies\n$$\\phi(x)\\geq-\\psi(|x|_\\infty),\\qquad \\int_0^\\infty\\psi(r)r^{d-1}\\,dr<\\infty.$$\nIt is regular if it is lower regular and, for some $R<\\infty$, $\\phi(x)\\leq\\psi(|x|_\\infty)$ whenever $|x|_\\infty\\geq R$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "1.3",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-1",
          "claim": "Since $\\psi$ is nonincreasing, $0\\leq g^d\\psi(g)\\leq \\frac{d}{1-2^{-d}}\\int_{g/2}^{g}r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr$ for $g>2R_0$: on $[g/2,g]$, $\\psi(r)\\geq\\psi(g)$, and integration of $r^{d-1}$ gives the displayed coefficient. Both the interval integral and the tail integral in $\\eta(g)$ tend to zero as $g\\to\\infty$, so $\\eta(g)\\to0$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-2",
          "claim": "For $m\\geq2$ and $r\\in[(m-1)g,mg]$, monotonicity gives $\\psi(r)\\geq\\psi(mg)$ and $r^{d-1}\\geq((m-1)g)^{d-1}$. Hence $$ \\int_{(m-1)g}^{mg}r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr\\geq g^d(m-1)^{d-1}\\psi(mg). $$ Since $m^{d-1}\\leq2^{d-1}(m-1)^{d-1}$, summing over disjoint intervals yields $\\sum_{m\\geq2}m^{d-1}\\psi(mg)\\leq2^{d-1}g^{-d}\\int_g^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr$. The $m=1$ term equals $g^{-d}g^d\\psi(g)$, so adding it proves the stated bound because $2^{d-1}\\geq1$.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-3",
          "claim": "For integer $m\\geq\\lceil R_0+3\\rceil$, monotonicity gives $\\psi(r)\\geq\\psi(m-1)$ on $[m-2,m-1]$, so $\\int_{m-2}^{m-1}r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr\\geq(m-2)^{d-1}\\psi(m-1)$. Since $m^{d-1}\\leq c_d(m-2)^{d-1}$ for these $m$, summing over disjoint unit intervals proves $\\sum_{m\\geq\\lceil R_0+3\\rceil} m^{d-1}\\psi(m-1)<\\infty$.",
          "step": "1.3",
          "inputs": [
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-1",
          "claim": "For each integer $k\\geq1$, let $G_k$ be the least integer greater than $2R_0$ such that $\\eta(g)\\leq k^{-2d}$ for every $g\\geq G_k$; it exists by step 1.1 and the well-ordering of the positive integers. Choose a strictly increasing sequence $L_k$ with $L_k\\geq kG_k$ and $L_k\\geq k^2$. For $\\ell\\geq L_1$, let $k(\\ell)=\\max\\{k:L_k\\leq\\ell\\}$ and $g(\\ell)=\\ell/k(\\ell)$. Then $k(\\ell)\\to\\infty$, $g(\\ell)\\geq G_{k(\\ell)}$ and $g(\\ell)\\geq k(\\ell)$, while $g(\\ell)/\\ell=1/k(\\ell)$. Therefore $$ \\left(\\frac{\\ell}{g(\\ell)}\\right)^d\\eta(g(\\ell))\\leq k(\\ell)^d k(\\ell)^{-2d}=k(\\ell)^{-d}\\to0. $$ This gives all three gap limits.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-3-1",
          "claim": "Fix distinct points $x,y$ in a finite configuration and a period $L>0$. For $|k|_\\infty$ larger than $2|x-y|_\\infty/L+2R_0/L$, the triangle inequality gives $|x-y+Lk|_\\infty\\geq L|k|_\\infty/2>2R_0$. Grouping lattice indices by $m=|k|_\\infty$ and applying the sum bound of step 1.2 with gap $g=L/2$ shows $\\sum_k|\\phi(x-y+Lk)|<\\infty$ whenever $L/2>2R_0$. There are finitely many remaining images; any $+\\infty$ term makes the periodic energy $+\\infty$ by definition, while otherwise their finite sum is well-defined. This proves the periodic-image convention used in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]] for all sufficiently large $L$.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "step 1.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "finite_checks": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement the cross-block pair estimates admit blocks containing no points: all pair contributions and quadratic occupation counts then vanish. The indexed offsets remain an actual integer lattice in d>=1.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $d\\geq1$ and let $\\phi$ be a regular potential with a nonnegative nonincreasing envelope $\\psi:[R_0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$, where $R_0<\\infty$ and $\\int_{R_0}^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr<\\infty$. Thus $|\\phi(x)|\\leq\\psi(|x|_\\infty)$ for $|x|_\\infty\\geq R_0$. For $g>2R_0$ set\n$$\\eta(g)=g^d\\psi(g)+\\int_g^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr.$$\nThen $\\eta(g)\\to0$ and\n$$\\sum_{m=1}^\\infty m^{d-1}\\psi(mg)\\leq 2^{d-1}g^{-d}\\eta(g).$$\nMoreover, there is a choice $g(\\ell)>0$, for all sufficiently large real $\\ell$, such that $g(\\ell)\\to\\infty$, $g(\\ell)/\\ell\\to0$, and\n$$\\left(\\frac{\\ell}{g(\\ell)}\\right)^d\\eta(g(\\ell))\\longrightarrow0.$$\nFor every fixed finite configuration and all sufficiently large periods $L$, the noncoincident periodic-image tail $\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^d,\\ |k|_\\infty\\geq K_0}|\\phi(x-y+Lk)|$ is absolutely convergent. The tail of the cell envelope $\\psi(|j|_\\infty-1)$ over all sufficiently large integer offsets is summable. This lemma is a deterministic tail estimate; it uses no superstability or thermodynamic-limit conclusion.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "7cd053716769f33464c5c7b8b841430c72f288269a61bfe1a7bcee71472d5302",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement the chosen tail gap is positive and tends to infinity, and g>2R_0 is used only in its tail regime. No estimate divides by a zero gap; an empty block contributes zero without division by its count.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $d\\geq1$ and let $\\phi$ be a regular potential with a nonnegative nonincreasing envelope $\\psi:[R_0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$, where $R_0<\\infty$ and $\\int_{R_0}^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr<\\infty$. Thus $|\\phi(x)|\\leq\\psi(|x|_\\infty)$ for $|x|_\\infty\\geq R_0$. For $g>2R_0$ set\n$$\\eta(g)=g^d\\psi(g)+\\int_g^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr.$$\nThen $\\eta(g)\\to0$ and\n$$\\sum_{m=1}^\\infty m^{d-1}\\psi(mg)\\leq 2^{d-1}g^{-d}\\eta(g).$$\nMoreover, there is a choice $g(\\ell)>0$, for all sufficiently large real $\\ell$, such that $g(\\ell)\\to\\infty$, $g(\\ell)/\\ell\\to0$, and\n$$\\left(\\frac{\\ell}{g(\\ell)}\\right)^d\\eta(g(\\ell))\\longrightarrow0.$$\nFor every fixed finite configuration and all sufficiently large periods $L$, the noncoincident periodic-image tail $\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^d,\\ |k|_\\infty\\geq K_0}|\\phi(x-y+Lk)|$ is absolutely convergent. The tail of the cell envelope $\\psi(|j|_\\infty-1)$ over all sufficiently large integer offsets is summable. This lemma is a deterministic tail estimate; it uses no superstability or thermodynamic-limit conclusion.",
