          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $\\phi=\\phi_s+\\phi_r$ be superstable in the splitting convention of [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]. Suppose $H_{\\phi_s}(\\omega)\\geq-B_sN(\\omega)$ and $\\phi_r(x)\\geq\\delta>0$ for $|x|_\\infty\\leq r_0$, with $\\phi_r\\geq0$ elsewhere. For the unit cells $C_i=i+[0,1)^d$, there are constants $A>0$ and $B\\geq0$ such that every finite configuration satisfies\n$$H_\\phi(\\omega)\\geq A\\sum_{i\\in\\mathbb Z^d}N_{C_i}(\\omega)^2-BN(\\omega).$$\nOnly finitely many summands are nonzero. This is the cell form used in the continuum pressure arguments.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "2bd0b076da82ffb7ccb1a9db8e7a0b335848e7b6bf7d3dfdbd5e6d457afbc53d",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-reverse",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Let $\\phi=\\phi_s+\\phi_r$ be superstable in the splitting convention of [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]. Boundary iff-reverse: The Statement is a one-way implication or limit assertion, not an equivalence.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $\\phi=\\phi_s+\\phi_r$ be superstable in the splitting convention of [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]. Suppose $H_{\\phi_s}(\\omega)\\geq-B_sN(\\omega)$ and $\\phi_r(x)\\geq\\delta>0$ for $|x|_\\infty\\leq r_0$, with $\\phi_r\\geq0$ elsewhere. For the unit cells $C_i=i+[0,1)^d$, there are constants $A>0$ and $B\\geq0$ such that every finite configuration satisfies\n$$H_\\phi(\\omega)\\geq A\\sum_{i\\in\\mathbb Z^d}N_{C_i}(\\omega)^2-BN(\\omega).$$\nOnly finitely many summands are nonzero. This is the cell form used in the continuum pressure arguments.",
