          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "For $L>0$ and a finite configuration $\\omega\\subset\\Lambda_L$ with $N(\\omega)=N$, the measure $R_{L,\\omega}$ of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]] is a stationary probability law of finite intensity and\n$$\\rho(R_{L,\\omega})=\\frac{N}{L^d}.$$\nFor any probability law $C_L$ on finite configurations in $\\Lambda_L$ with $E_{C_L}N<\\infty$, its empirical-field barycenter $\\bar C_L$ is also a stationary probability law of finite intensity and $\\rho(\\bar C_L)=E_{C_L}N/L^d$. Boundary zero: The Statement fixes positive parameters or has no zero-parameter conclusion; the zero case is outside this claim.",
          "case_scope": {
