    "thm-tdmath-superstable-van-hove-pressure": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "With fixed numerical length and energy units, the canonical positional partition is\n$$Z(L,N;\\beta)=\\frac1{N!}\\int_{\\Lambda_L^N}e^{-\\beta H_\\phi(q_1,\\ldots,q_N)}dq_1\\cdots dq_N,\\quad Z(L,0;\\beta)=1,$$\nwhere $\\beta>0$, and the grand partition is $\\Xi(L;a,\\beta)=\\sum_{N\\geq0}a^NZ(L,N;\\beta)$ for numerical activity $a>0$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-tdmath-van-hove-sequence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a bounded set $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ and $R>0$, define its two-sided boundary layer\n$$\\partial_R\\Omega=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\operatorname{dist}(x,\\partial\\Omega)\\leq R\\},$$\nwhere distance is Euclidean distance and $|\\cdot|$ denotes $d$-dimensional Lebesgue measure.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-superstable-cell-energy-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For the unit cells $C_i=i+[0,1)^d$, there are constants $A>0$ and $B\\geq0$ such that every finite configuration satisfies\n$$H_\\phi(\\omega)\\geq A\\sum_{i\\in\\mathbb Z^d}N_{C_i}(\\omega)^2-BN(\\omega).$$\nOnly finitely many summands are nonzero.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-decreasing-integrable-tail-free-cube-pressure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For free-boundary cubes define $\\Xi_L(a,\\beta)=\\sum_{N\\geq0}a^NZ(L,N;\\beta)$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ and $(Y,\\mathcal B,\\nu)$ be sigma-finite measure\nspaces, and let $f : X \\times Y \\to [0,\\infty]$ be product-measurable.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-1",
          "claim": "First take a finite union $\\mathcal R$ of unit cells and its free Gibbs law. By [L1] and Tonelli [F5],\n$$E N_i^2=E N_i+E[N_i(N_i-1)] \\leq \\xi |C_i\\cap\\mathcal R|+\\xi^2|C_i\\cap\\mathcal R|^2 \\leq M:=\\xi+\\xi^2.$$\nLet the cells be partitioned into boxes of side $\\ell$. For each cell $i$, let $e_i$ be the sum of the lower-regular lattice envelope over cells $j$ in other boxes. The negative cross-box energy obeys $W^-\\leq\\tfrac12\\sum_i e_iN_i^2$, because $N_iN_j\\leq(N_i^2+N_j^2)/2$. Therefore $E W^-\\leq(M/2)\\sum_i e_i$. If $\\sum_i e_i>0$, then $P(W^->M\\sum_i e_i)\\leq E W^-/(M\\sum_i e_i)\\leq1/2$; if the sum is zero, $W^-=0$ almost surely. Thus the event $W^-\\leq M\\sum_i e_i$ has probability at least $1/2$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "L1",
            "F5",
            "F1",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-1",
          "claim": "For each $\\Omega_k$, let $\\mathcal R_k$ be the union of unit cells meeting $\\Omega_k$. Then $\\Xi_{\\Omega_k}\\leq\\Xi_{\\mathcal R_k}$ by domain monotonicity, and $|\\mathcal R_k|/|\\Omega_k|\\to1$ by the van Hove boundary condition. Partition $\\mathcal R_k$ into boxes of $\\ell$ unit cells per side. The probability event from step 1.1 has full Gibbs probability at least $1/2$; on it, $H_{\\mathrm{total}}\\geq H_{\\mathrm{in}}-M\\sum_i e_i$, where $H_{\\mathrm{in}}$ is the sum of within-box energies. Therefore\n$$\\Xi_{\\mathcal R_k}/2\\leq e^{\\beta M\\sum_i e_i}\\prod_B\\Xi_{\\mathcal R_k\\cap B}.$$\nIndeed, $\\Xi_{\\mathcal R_k}\\mu_{\\mathcal R_k}(E)=\\int_Ee^{-\\beta H_{\\mathrm{total}}}d\\Pi\\leq e^{\\beta M\\sum_i e_i}\\int_Ee^{-\\beta H_{\\mathrm{in}}}d\\Pi$, and the last integral is bounded by the unrestricted product over boxes. Each partial-box partition is at most the full $\\ell$-cube partition. For one full box, $E_\\ell=\\sum_{i\\in B,j\\notin B}\\Psi(|i-j|)$ satisfies $E_\\ell/\\ell^d\\to0$: cells within fixed distance $R$ of the boundary are $O_R(\\ell^{d-1})$; all other cells contribute at most the summable tail beyond $R$. Thus\n$$\\limsup_k|\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log\\Xi_{\\Omega_k} \\leq\\ell^{-d}\\bigl[\\log\\Xi_{\\Lambda_\\ell}+\\beta M E_\\ell\\bigr].$$\nLet $\\ell\\to\\infty$ and use [F4].",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F4",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F5",
            "L1",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-3-1",
          "claim": "For the lower bound, fix core side $\\ell$ and gap $g$, and retain every whole $(\\ell+g)$-cell whose core lies in $\\Omega_k$. By the van Hove property [F2], the retained count divided by $|\\Omega_k|$ tends $(\\ell+g)^{-d}$. Restrict each core to at most $K\\ell^d$ particles. Exact $N!$ cancellation factorizes their grand weights. The lattice-shell count and [F1] bound positive cross energy per core by $C K^2(\\ell/g)^d\\eta(g)$, with $\\eta(g)\\to0$ from the integrable tail. This gives the same separated-core lower bound as the free-cube packing proof. First let $k\\to\\infty$, then choose $g=g(\\ell)$ from [[lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap]] and let $\\ell\\to\\infty$; packing fraction tends one and the cross penalty vanishes. The resulting liminf is at least the cube pressure [F4].",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F1",
            "F4",
            "step 2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "finite_checks": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Assume a superstable regular pair potential as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]] and the van Hove definition [[def-tdmath-van-hove-sequence]]. Boundary empty: The Statement has no empty-configuration branch; its claim concerns the displayed positive-volume, density, or conditional regime.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume a superstable regular pair potential as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]] and the van Hove definition [[def-tdmath-van-hove-sequence]]. For every van Hove sequence $(\\Omega_k)$, the free-wall physical grand pressure satisfies\n$$|\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log\\Xi_{\\Omega_k}(z,\\beta)\\longrightarrow p(z,\\beta),$$\nthe free-cube limit from [[thm-tdmath-decreasing-integrable-tail-free-cube-pressure]]. The extra superstability hypothesis is essential to this proof's uniform cell-occupation bound; no arbitrary-shape theorem under stability alone is claimed.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "dbb5701ffda53f9325ef7efff5f6877b601428977f545c1a9844c453ea6cc732",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
