      "external_sources": {
        "L1": {
          "title": "D. Ruelle, Superstable Interactions in Classical Statistical Mechanics",
          "url": "https://www.ihes.fr/~ruelle/PUBLICATIONS/%5B28%5D.pdf",
          "source_section": "Section 6, printed pp.188–191 / PDF pp.18–21; complete relevant arguments and the Ruelle moment proof were read.",
          "source_statement": "For a superstable lower-regular interaction, finite-volume and tempered-law estimates control near-boundary and far-tail contributions uniformly over the stated square-count class.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-local-tame-entropy-compactness",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1",
            "2.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The normalized unit-intensity Poisson version is $Z_Q(L;z,\\beta)=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,\\mathrm{free}}}]$; since the Poisson density contributes $e^{-V_L}$, $\\Xi(L;z,\\beta)=e^{V_L}Z_Q(L;z,\\beta)$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-superstable-cell-energy-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For the unit cells $C_i=i+[0,1)^d$, there are constants $A>0$ and $B\\geq0$ such that every finite configuration satisfies\n$$H_\\phi(\\omega)\\geq A\\sum_{i\\in\\mathbb Z^d}N_{C_i}(\\omega)^2-BN(\\omega).$$\nOnly finitely many summands are nonzero.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-local-tame-entropy-compactness",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Then $\\mathcal H_c$ is compact and sequentially compact in $\\tau_L$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1",
            "2.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-spatial-mean-information",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $d\\geq1$, let $P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}(\\Omega)$, with this class defined in [[def-tdmath-local-tame-topology]], be ergodic under the full translation group $\\mathbb R^d$, and suppose its specific relative entropy $I(P)=\\gamma$ relative to the unit-intensity Poisson law $Q$ is finite.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "def-tdmath-local-tame-topology",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A real measurable function $f$ on $\\Omega$ is local if there is a bounded Borel set $A$ such that $f$ is measurable with respect to the restriction $\\omega\\mapsto\\omega|_A$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-decreasing-integrable-tail-free-cube-pressure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\phi$ be stable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], with stability constant $B$, and fix $a,\\beta>0$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-monotone-convergence-for-the-integral",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $0\\le f_1\\le f_2\\le\\cdots$ be measurable and suppose $f_n(x)\\uparrow f(x)$\nfor every $x$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-relative-entropy-variational-and-chain-rules",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Then\n$$D(P_{XY}\\Vert Q_X\\otimes Q_Y)=D(P_X\\Vert Q_X)+\\int_X D(P_{Y|X=x}\\Vert Q_Y)\\,P_X(dx).$$\nMore generally, for nested standard-Borel observations $R$ and $S$ with $R$ a measurable function of $S$, and a fixed probability reference $Q_Y$ for a further variable $Y$, the conditional increments\n$$G(R):=E_P\\!\\left[D(P_{Y|R}\\Vert Q_Y)\\right],\\qquad G(S):=E_P\\!\\left[D(P_{Y|S}\\Vert Q_Y)\\right]$$\nsatisfy $0\\leq G(R)\\leq G(S)$ whenever the joint relative entropy is finite.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "def-tdmath-finite-region-relative-entropy",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "If $P$ and $Q$ are probability measures on the same measurable space, define\n$$D(P\\Vert Q)=\\begin{cases}\\displaystyle\\int h\\log h\\,dQ,&P\\ll Q\\text{ and }h=dP/dQ,\\\\+\\infty,&P\\not\\ll Q.\\end{cases}$$\nUse $0\\log0=0$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-1",
          "claim": "Georgii's Theorem 1 [L1] gives existence of $\\Phi(P)$ and lower semicontinuity for every stationary finite-intensity law. Its Euclidean radial tail hypothesis follows from ours: $|x|_\\infty\\leq|x|_2\\leq\\sqrt d\\,|x|_\\infty$, so replacing $\\psi(r)$ by $\\psi(r/\\sqrt d)$ preserves monotonicity and finite weighted integral by a change of variables. The stable-plus-positive-core definition matches the source's superstable condition after choosing a smaller Euclidean core ball. Thus $\\Phi$ has exactly the domain and convention in the Statement.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "L1",
            "F1",
            "F2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-2",
          "claim": "The cell estimate [F2] and $\\beta>0$ imply $J=I+\\beta\\Phi-\\rho\\log z$ is lower semicontinuous and coercive on bounded-$J$ sets: the Poisson entropy variational inequality with bounded truncations of $aN_{C_0}$ gives $I(P)\\geq a\\rho(P)-(e^a-1)$; the pointwise square inequality gives $E_PN_{C_0}^2\\geq\\rho(P)^2$. Hence bounded $J$ bounds $\\rho$, $I$, and $\\Phi$ from above. A finite candidate exists: take independent Bernoulli occupancy of widely separated small cubes, at most one absolutely continuously distributed point per cube, and a uniform random lattice phase. Each tile has finite relative entropy to Poisson, and the summable regular tail bounds its absolute intertile energy per volume. Thus $J$ is proper. By [F3] and the choice assumptions [A1], its bounded sublevels are compact in $\\tau_L$.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "F7",
            "F8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-1",
          "claim": "For the finite-volume Gibbs tilt $G_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$, direct integration gives $$ L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc} =-L^{-d}D(G_{L,z,\\beta,bc}\\Vert Q_{\\Lambda_L}) -\\beta L^{-d}E_GH_{L,bc} +L^{-d}\\log z\\,E_GN. $$ Georgii's Theorem 2 [L2], applied with the present superstable regular interaction and $F=0$, supplies the matching upper and lower empirical-field bounds and the free/periodic pressure limit. Its upper proof uses this entropy identity, block stationarization, and the superstable cell cutoff; its lower proof conditions finite blocks on bounded finite-energy events, inserts empty corridors, and applies the spatial likelihood limit. The inspected source hypotheses match [F1]–[F8]: the Poisson reference is independent unit intensity, $\\tau_L$ is the local-tame topology [F5], entropy compactness is [F3], and the energy-density interface is [L1]. The theorem therefore yields $$ p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_P\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\} $$ for both boundary conditions, with compact variational sublevels.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "L2",
            "F1",
            "F8",
            "F5",
            "F3",
            "L1",
            "A1",
            "F4",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-2",
          "claim": "The minimum is attained: a minimizing sequence lies in a finite sublevel by the sparse finite candidate in step 1.2; compactness [F3] gives a convergent subsequence and lower semicontinuity from step 1.1 gives a minimizer. The set of minimizers is the closed minimum level within that compact sublevel, hence nonempty and compact. This agrees with the compact-sublevel conclusion in [L2].",
          "step": "2.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F3",
            "L2",
            "A1",
            "step 1.2",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-3-1",
          "claim": "The unit-intensity Poisson law on $\\Lambda_L$ has density $e^{-L^d}/N!$ relative to Lebesgue measure on the $N$-point sector. Therefore the physical partition $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}=e^{L^d}Z_{L,z,\\beta,\\mathrm{free}}$; its log rate is $p_Q+1$. This is only a positional normalization conversion.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F6",
            "L2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "finite_checks": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement/Example scope: Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. Case empty: step 2.1 addresses the empty case.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB. Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. For stationary finite-intensity configuration laws, let $I(P)$ be relative entropy density with respect to the independent unit-intensity Poisson law, $\\rho(P)=E_PN_{[0,1)^d}$, and $\\Phi(P)$ the limiting positional energy density. The existence and lower semicontinuity of $\\Phi$ under these hypotheses are part of the proof below. For free and periodic cubes define\n$$Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}\\!\\left[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,bc}}\\right],\\qquad bc\\in\\{\\mathrm{free},\\mathrm{per}\\}.$$\nThen the limit $p_Q(z,\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$ exists, is independent of $bc$, and\n$$p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThe minimizer set is nonempty and compact in the local-tame topology $\\tau_L$. This theorem concerns positional configurations only. If $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}$ is instead normalized against Lebesgue measure with $1/N!$, then $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}=e^{L^d}Z_{L,z,\\beta,\\mathrm{free}}$, so its logarithmic rate is $p_Q+1$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "d5006093bd1b2359fef76a6820c9af9838fbeded40043bdb2c79b4b4b03fa261",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement/Example scope: Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. Case zero: step 1.2 addresses the zero case.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB. Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. For stationary finite-intensity configuration laws, let $I(P)$ be relative entropy density with respect to the independent unit-intensity Poisson law, $\\rho(P)=E_PN_{[0,1)^d}$, and $\\Phi(P)$ the limiting positional energy density. The existence and lower semicontinuity of $\\Phi$ under these hypotheses are part of the proof below. For free and periodic cubes define\n$$Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}\\!\\left[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,bc}}\\right],\\qquad bc\\in\\{\\mathrm{free},\\mathrm{per}\\}.$$\nThen the limit $p_Q(z,\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$ exists, is independent of $bc$, and\n$$p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThe minimizer set is nonempty and compact in the local-tame topology $\\tau_L$. This theorem concerns positional configurations only. If $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}$ is instead normalized against Lebesgue measure with $1/N!$, then $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}=e^{L^d}Z_{L,z,\\beta,\\mathrm{free}}$, so its logarithmic rate is $p_Q+1$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "d5006093bd1b2359fef76a6820c9af9838fbeded40043bdb2c79b4b4b03fa261",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. Boundary one: The result is an asymptotic or general-law claim and makes no separate one-particle assertion.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB. Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. For stationary finite-intensity configuration laws, let $I(P)$ be relative entropy density with respect to the independent unit-intensity Poisson law, $\\rho(P)=E_PN_{[0,1)^d}$, and $\\Phi(P)$ the limiting positional energy density. The existence and lower semicontinuity of $\\Phi$ under these hypotheses are part of the proof below. For free and periodic cubes define\n$$Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}\\!\\left[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,bc}}\\right],\\qquad bc\\in\\{\\mathrm{free},\\mathrm{per}\\}.$$\nThen the limit $p_Q(z,\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$ exists, is independent of $bc$, and\n$$p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThe minimizer set is nonempty and compact in the local-tame topology $\\tau_L$. This theorem concerns positional configurations only. If $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}$ is instead normalized against Lebesgue measure with $1/N!$, then $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}=e^{L^d}Z_{L,z,\\beta,\\mathrm{free}}$, so its logarithmic rate is $p_Q+1$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "d5006093bd1b2359fef76a6820c9af9838fbeded40043bdb2c79b4b4b03fa261",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. Boundary degenerate: The Statement contains no degeneracy, differentiability, or uniqueness case.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB. Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and fix $z,\\beta>0$. For stationary finite-intensity configuration laws, let $I(P)$ be relative entropy density with respect to the independent unit-intensity Poisson law, $\\rho(P)=E_PN_{[0,1)^d}$, and $\\Phi(P)$ the limiting positional energy density. The existence and lower semicontinuity of $\\Phi$ under these hypotheses are part of the proof below. For free and periodic cubes define\n$$Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}\\!\\left[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,bc}}\\right],\\qquad bc\\in\\{\\mathrm{free},\\mathrm{per}\\}.$$\nThen the limit $p_Q(z,\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$ exists, is independent of $bc$, and\n$$p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThe minimizer set is nonempty and compact in the local-tame topology $\\tau_L$. This theorem concerns positional configurations only. If $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}$ is instead normalized against Lebesgue measure with $1/N!$, then $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}=e^{L^d}Z_{L,z,\\beta,\\mathrm{free}}$, so its logarithmic rate is $p_Q+1$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "d5006093bd1b2359fef76a6820c9af9838fbeded40043bdb2c79b4b4b03fa261",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
