      ],
      "external_sources": {
        "L1": {
          "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
          "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
          "source_section": "Theorem 1, Section 3, printed p.174 / PDF p.4.",
          "source_statement": "Suppose φ is superstable and lower regular. Then, for each P, the limit of the expected energy density exists and is lower semicontinuous.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        "L2": {
          "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
          "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
          "source_section": "Theorem 2, Section 3, equations (2.20)–(2.22), printed pp.175–176 / PDF pp.5–6.",
          "source_statement": "For a superstable regular potential and z, β>0, the free and periodic partition rates agree with the stationary variational minimum, whose rate levels are compact.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "2.2",
            "3.1"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "thm-tdmath-van-hove-fixed-n-limit": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "With fixed numerical length and energy units, the canonical positional partition is\n$$Z(L,N;\\beta)=\\frac1{N!}\\int_{\\Lambda_L^N}e^{-\\beta H_\\phi(q_1,\\ldots,q_N)}dq_1\\cdots dq_N,\\quad Z(L,0;\\beta)=1,$$\nwhere $\\beta>0$, and the grand partition is $\\Xi(L;a,\\beta)=\\sum_{N\\geq0}a^NZ(L,N;\\beta)$ for numerical activity $a>0$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-tdmath-van-hove-sequence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A van Hove sequence is a sequence of bounded Lebesgue measurable sets $(\\Omega_k)_{k\\geq1}$ with $0<|\\Omega_k|<\\infty$, $|\\Omega_k|\\to\\infty$, and\n$$\\frac{|\\partial_R\\Omega_k|}{|\\Omega_k|}\\longrightarrow0\\qquad\\text{for every fixed }R>0.$$\nThe condition controls both inner and outer boundary neighborhoods.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For sequences $L_j\\to\\infty$ and integers $N_j\\geq0$ with $N_j/L_j^d\\to\\rho$, define\n$$b(\\rho)=\\sup\\left\\{\\limsup_{j\\to\\infty}L_j^{-d}\\log Z(L_j,N_j;\\beta):\\frac{N_j}{L_j^d}\\to\\rho\\right\\}.$$\nLet $F$ be the concave envelope of $b$ on $[0,\\infty)$, namely the supremum of $\\sum_{i=1}^m\\theta_i b(\\rho_i)$ over finite lists with $\\theta_i\\geq0$, $\\sum_i\\theta_i=1$, $\\rho_i\\geq0$, and $\\sum_i\\theta_i\\rho_i=\\rho$; the empty supremum is $-\\infty$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Then\n$$P(\\alpha,\\beta)=\\sup_{\\rho\\geq0}\\bigl(F_\\beta(\\rho)+\\alpha\\rho\\bigr),\\qquad F_\\beta(\\rho)=\\inf_{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R}\\bigl(P(\\alpha,\\beta)-\\alpha\\rho\\bigr)$$\nfor every $\\rho$ in the closed effective domain of $F_\\beta$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-superstable-van-hove-pressure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every van Hove sequence $(\\Omega_k)$, the free-wall physical grand pressure satisfies\n$$|\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log\\Xi_{\\Omega_k}(z,\\beta)\\longrightarrow p(z,\\beta),$$\nthe free-cube limit from [[thm-tdmath-decreasing-integrable-tail-free-cube-pressure]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $d\\geq1$ and let $\\phi$ be a regular potential with a nonnegative nonincreasing envelope $\\psi:[R_0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$, where $R_0<\\infty$ and $\\int_{R_0}^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr<\\infty$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "3.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-1",
          "claim": "For any $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R$, $e^{\\alpha N_k}Z(\\Omega_k,N_k)\\leq\\Xi_{\\Omega_k}(e^\\alpha,\\beta)$. Divide by volume, use [F5], and take the infimum over $\\alpha$. The duality [F4] gives $\\limsup |\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log Z(\\Omega_k,N_k)\\leq F_\\beta(\\rho)$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F5",
            "F4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-2",
          "claim": "Choose $\\delta>0$ so $\\rho-\\delta,\\rho+\\delta$ lie in the attainable interior. For large core side $\\ell$, choose integers $n_-,n_+$ with $n_\\pm/\\ell^d\\to\\rho\\pm\\delta$. Put a central $\\ell$-cube inside each $(\\ell+g)$-cell, with $g=g(\\ell)$ from [F6]. The effective densities $n_\\pm/(\\ell+g)^d$ still bracket $\\rho$ when $\\ell$ is large.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F6",
            "F2",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-1",
          "claim": "At fixed $\\ell,g$, pack every complete $(\\ell+g)$-cell contained in $\\Omega_k$. Its count $M_k$ satisfies $M_k/|\\Omega_k|\\to(\\ell+g)^{-d}$ by [F2]. Assign $n_+$ particles to $j_k$ cores and $n_-$ to the remaining cores, except one correction core with remainder $r_k$ chosen to make the total exactly $N_k$. Bracketing ensures $0\\leq j_k<M_k$ for large $k$; Euclidean division gives $0\\leq r_k<n_+-n_- \\leq n_+$. Every correction integral $Z(\\ell,r)$, $0\\leq r\\leq n_+$, is positive: delete particles from a positive-measure finite-energy set realizing $Z(\\ell,n_+)>0$. There are finitely many such $r$, so the correction contributes $O_\\ell(1)$ to the log weight.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F1",
            "step 1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-3-1",
          "claim": "Exact assignment of labels cancels the global $N_k!$, leaving the product of core canonical integrals. The core lattice shell estimate bounds cross-energy per volume by $C K^2(\\ell/g)^d\\eta(g)$, where $K\\ell^d\\geq n_+$. Let $k\\to\\infty$ first, then $\\ell\\to\\infty$. The packing fraction tends one, the cross error tends zero, and the two rates tend $F_\\beta(\\rho-\\delta)$ and $F_\\beta(\\rho+\\delta)$. The bracketing proportions tend one half, so the lower rate is at least their average. Finally $\\delta\\downarrow0$; finite concavity makes $F_\\beta$ continuous at the interior density. Combined with step 1.1 this proves the limit.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F6",
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "finite_checks": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Assume superstability and regularity, let $(\\Omega_k)$ be van Hove, and let $N_k/|\\Omega_k|\\to\\rho$ for an interior attainable density $\\rho>0$. Boundary empty: The Statement has no empty-configuration branch; its claim concerns the displayed positive-volume, density, or conditional regime.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume superstability and regularity, let $(\\Omega_k)$ be van Hove, and let $N_k/|\\Omega_k|\\to\\rho$ for an interior attainable density $\\rho>0$. For the free-wall exact-$N_k$ positional partition with $1/N_k!$ normalization,\n$$|\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log Z(\\Omega_k,N_k;\\beta)\\longrightarrow F_\\beta(\\rho),$$\nthe free-cube canonical rate of [[thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit]]. Superstability is used for the arbitrary-shape pressure upper bound; no stability-only upper theorem is asserted.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "eeff5ef721582012d99adebd237f29d08cb2db52a51c0ec2b9a3950fff8466dc",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
