          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume superstability and regularity, let $(\\Omega_k)$ be van Hove, and let $N_k/|\\Omega_k|\\to\\rho$ for an interior attainable density $\\rho>0$. For the free-wall exact-$N_k$ positional partition with $1/N_k!$ normalization,\n$$|\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log Z(\\Omega_k,N_k;\\beta)\\longrightarrow F_\\beta(\\rho),$$\nthe free-cube canonical rate of [[thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit]]. Superstability is used for the arbitrary-shape pressure upper bound; no stability-only upper theorem is asserted.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "eeff5ef721582012d99adebd237f29d08cb2db52a51c0ec2b9a3950fff8466dc",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "lem-tdmath-canonical-empirical-field-conditioning": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "With fixed numerical length and energy units, the canonical positional partition is\n$$Z(L,N;\\beta)=\\frac1{N!}\\int_{\\Lambda_L^N}e^{-\\beta H_\\phi(q_1,\\ldots,q_N)}dq_1\\cdots dq_N,\\quad Z(L,0;\\beta)=1,$$\nwhere $\\beta>0$, and the grand partition is $\\Xi(L;a,\\beta)=\\sum_{N\\geq0}a^NZ(L,N;\\beta)$ for numerical activity $a>0$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R$, define\n$$P(\\alpha,\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log\\Xi_L(e^\\alpha,\\beta),$$\nwhose existence is [[thm-tdmath-decreasing-integrable-tail-free-cube-pressure]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For free and periodic cubes define\n$$Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}\\!\\left[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,bc}}\\right],\\qquad bc\\in\\{\\mathrm{free},\\mathrm{per}\\}.$$\nThen the limit $p_Q(z,\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$ exists, is independent of $bc$, and\n$$p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThe minimizer set is nonempty and compact in the local-tame topology $\\tau_L$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Define its **periodized empirical field**\n$$R_{L,\\omega}:=\\frac1{L^d}\\int_{\\Lambda_L}\\delta_{T_x\\omega^{(L)}}\\,dx.$$\nThe integral is the push-forward of normalized Lebesgue measure on $\\Lambda_L$ under $x\\mapsto T_x\\omega^{(L)}$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field-stationary-density",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $L>0$ and a finite configuration $\\omega\\subset\\Lambda_L$ with $N(\\omega)=N$, the measure $R_{L,\\omega}$ of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]] is a stationary probability law of finite intensity and\n$$\\rho(R_{L,\\omega})=\\frac{N}{L^d}.$$\nFor any probability law $C_L$ on finite configurations in $\\Lambda_L$ with $E_{C_L}N<\\infty$, its empirical-field barycenter $\\bar C_L$ is also a stationary probability law of finite intensity and $\\rho(\\bar C_L)=E_{C_L}N/L^d$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-1",
          "claim": "The canonical law is the grand law conditioned on $N=N_L$, since the grand weight on the $N_L$ sector differs from the canonical density only by the constant activity factor $z^{N_L}$. Its conditioning probability is $$G^b_{L,z,\\beta}(N=N_L)=\\frac{z^{N_L}e^{-L^d}Z_b(L,N_L;\\beta)}{Z_{Q,b}(L;z,\\beta)}.$$ Divide the logarithm by $L^d$. The numerator terms tend to $\\rho\\log z+F_\\beta(\\rho)-1$ by the assumed canonical rate and [F1]; the denominator tends to $p_Q(z,\\beta)$. By [F2]–[F3], $p_Q(z,\\beta)=F_\\beta(\\rho)+\\rho\\log z-1$, so $$L^{-d}\\log G^b_{L,z,\\beta}(N=N_L)\\longrightarrow0.$$ Thus the exact-number conditioning event has subexponential, positive grand probability for all sufficiently large $L$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-2",
          "claim": "Let $U$ be an open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood of $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$ and set $F=U^c$. The good rate in [L1] has zero set exactly $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$. Its infimum on the closed set $F$ is strictly positive: otherwise a sequence in $F$ with rates tending to zero would lie in a compact rate sublevel, have a limit in $F$, and by lower semicontinuity that limit would be a zero of the rate outside $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$. The large-deviation upper bound therefore gives some $c>0$ with $$\\limsup_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log G^b_{L,z,\\beta}\\{R_{L,\\omega}\\in F\\}\\leq-c.$$",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "L1",
            "F3",
            "F4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-1",
          "claim": "Conditioning on $N=N_L$ yields $$C^b_{L,N_L}\\{R_{L,\\omega}\\notin U\\}\\leq \\frac{G^b_{L,z,\\beta}\\{R_{L,\\omega}\\in F\\}}{G^b_{L,z,\\beta}(N=N_L)}.$$ The numerator decays exponentially by step 1.2 and the denominator has zero exponential rate by step 1.1, so the ratio tends to zero. This proves concentration on every neighborhood of $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$. If the minimizer is unique, these neighborhood bounds are exactly convergence in probability in $\\tau_L$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.2",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "finite_checks": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Let $\\beta,z>0$, let $\\rho>0$ be an interior attainable density, and choose $\\alpha=\\log z$ supporting the free canonical rate $F_\\beta$ at $\\rho$. Boundary empty: The Statement has no empty-configuration branch; its claim concerns the displayed positive-volume, density, or conditional regime.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $\\beta,z>0$, let $\\rho>0$ be an interior attainable density, and choose $\\alpha=\\log z$ supporting the free canonical rate $F_\\beta$ at $\\rho$. For either free or periodic boundary condition $b$, let $C^b_{L,N_L}$ be the exact-$N_L$ canonical law and $G^b_{L,z,\\beta}$ the grand-canonical law using the same finite-volume energy, where $N_L/L^d\\to\\rho$. Assume\n$$L^{-d}\\log Z_b(L,N_L;\\beta)\\longrightarrow F_\\beta(\\rho).$$\nLet $R_{L,\\omega}$ be the periodized empirical field of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]], and let\n$$\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}:=\\operatorname*{argmin}_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThen for every open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood $U$ of $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$ there is $c_U>0$ such that\n$$\\limsup_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log C^b_{L,N_L}\\{\\,\\omega:R_{L,\\omega}\\notin U\\,\\}\\leq-c_U.$$\nIf $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}=\\{P_*\\}$, then $R_{L,\\omega}\\to P_*$ in probability in $\\tau_L$ under $C^b_{L,N_L}$. This is a statement about spatially averaged local observables through the empirical field, not about the raw finite-box law at a fixed origin.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "cfbd2b5bb3370649285f333068ff0a1da5f2a3e24f38561cea48b78a325f05cb",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
