      ],
      "external_sources": {
        "L1": {
          "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
          "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
          "source_section": "Theorem 4, Section 7, printed pp.177–178 / PDF pp.7–8; complete proof read.",
          "source_statement": "For a superstable regular interaction, nondegenerate D with inf D<ν(φ), and e>inf φ(D), the periodic upper-energy event has the stated entropy exponent and common variational minimizers.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "thm-tdmath-periodic-fixed-n-limit": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The far image sum is absolutely convergent for all sufficiently large $L$ by [[lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap]]; this is the image convention used below.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The tail of the cell envelope $\\psi(|j|_\\infty-1)$ over all sufficiently large integer offsets is summable.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-superstable-cell-energy-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For the unit cells $C_i=i+[0,1)^d$, there are constants $A>0$ and $B\\geq0$ such that every finite configuration satisfies\n$$H_\\phi(\\omega)\\geq A\\sum_{i\\in\\mathbb Z^d}N_{C_i}(\\omega)^2-BN(\\omega).$$\nOnly finitely many summands are nonzero.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every $\\rho>0$ in that interior and every such sequence $(L_j,N_j)$,\n$$\\lim_{j\\to\\infty}L_j^{-d}\\log Z(L_j,N_j;\\beta)=F(\\rho).$$\nNo claim is made at a close-packing endpoint or at any other excluded endpoint.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $F_\\beta$ be the finite concave canonical rate on the interior attainable-density interval from [[thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For free and periodic cubes define\n$$Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}\\!\\left[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,bc}}\\right],\\qquad bc\\in\\{\\mathrm{free},\\mathrm{per}\\}.$$\nThen the limit $p_Q(z,\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$ exists, is independent of $bc$, and\n$$p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThe minimizer set is nonempty and compact in the local-tame topology $\\tau_L$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-canonical-empirical-field-conditioning",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For either free or periodic boundary condition $b$, let $C^b_{L,N_L}$ be the exact-$N_L$ canonical law and $G^b_{L,z,\\beta}$ the grand-canonical law using the same finite-volume energy, where $N_L/L^d\\to\\rho$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "thm-holder-inequality-for-integrals",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ be a measure space, let $p,q\\in[1,\\infty]$ be\nconjugate exponents, and let $f,g$ be measurable real-valued functions.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F9",
          "source": "def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Define its **periodized empirical field**\n$$R_{L,\\omega}:=\\frac1{L^d}\\int_{\\Lambda_L}\\delta_{T_x\\omega^{(L)}}\\,dx.$$\nThe integral is the push-forward of normalized Lebesgue measure on $\\Lambda_L$ under $x\\mapsto T_x\\omega^{(L)}$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F9",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field-stationary-density",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $L>0$ and a finite configuration $\\omega\\subset\\Lambda_L$ with $N(\\omega)=N$, the measure $R_{L,\\omega}$ of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]] is a stationary probability law of finite intensity and\n$$\\rho(R_{L,\\omega})=\\frac{N}{L^d}.$$\nFor any probability law $C_L$ on finite configurations in $\\Lambda_L$ with $E_{C_L}N<\\infty$, its empirical-field barycenter $\\bar C_L$ is also a stationary probability law of finite intensity and $\\rho(\\bar C_L)=E_{C_L}N/L^d$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-1",
          "claim": "For the upper bound, $e^{\\alpha N_L}Z_{\\mathrm{per}}(L,N_L;\\beta)\\leq\\Xi_{\\mathrm{per}}(L,e^\\alpha,\\beta)$ for every real $\\alpha$. Divide logarithms by $L^d$, use the free/periodic grand limit [F6], and then take the infimum over $\\alpha$. The canonical-grand duality [F5] gives $\\limsup L^{-d}\\log Z_{\\mathrm{per}}\\leq F_\\beta(\\rho)$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F6",
            "F5",
            "F4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-2",
          "claim": "Fix corridor width $k$ larger than the tail cutoff. Restrict the $N_L$ particles to the inner cube of side $L-k$, leaving the corridor empty. The exact-$N_L$ density is still $\\rho$. The diagonal-gap supplier [F2] gives the vanishing regular-tail cutoff used here. By [L1], the periodized energy differs from the free inner-cube energy by at most $c_d\\delta_kT_{L-k}$. The cell bound [F3] implies $T_{L-k}\\leq A^{-1}(H_{L-k}+BN_L)$. Consequently $$ Z_{\\mathrm{per}}(L,N_L;\\beta)\\geq e^{-\\beta c_d\\delta_k BN_L/A}\\, Z(L-k,N_L;\\beta(1+c_d\\delta_k/A)). $$ The canonical theorem [F4] applies at the perturbed inverse temperature, giving the corresponding lower rate.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "L1",
            "F3",
            "F4",
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-1",
          "claim": "At fixed interior $\\rho$, $F_\\beta(\\rho)$ is finite and convex as a function of $\\beta>0$, by Hölder’s inequality [F8], since each finite-volume log partition is convex and the pointwise limit is finite. A finite convex function is continuous on the open interval: on a compact subinterval, its secant slopes are bounded by the slopes to fixed exterior endpoints. Let $L\\to\\infty$ in step 1.2 and then $k\\to\\infty$, so $\\delta_k\\to0$; continuity yields $\\liminf\\geq F_\\beta(\\rho)$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F8",
            "F4",
            "step 1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-3-1",
          "claim": "Step 2.1 established the periodic exact-$N_L$ rate $F_\\beta(\\rho)$, and [F5] supplies a finite supporting activity. The grand rate in [F6] and the periodized empirical field in [F9] satisfy the hypotheses of [F7] with periodic boundary condition. Hence the periodic empirical fields concentrate near the minimizer set, and concentrate at its singleton when it is unique.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F5",
            "F6",
            "F9",
            "F7",
            "step 2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
