          "evidence": "Statement/Example scope: Assume the superstable regular interaction of [[thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure]], $\\beta>0$, and an interior attainable density $\\rho>0$. Case empty: step 1.2 addresses the empty case.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume the superstable regular interaction of [[thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure]], $\\beta>0$, and an interior attainable density $\\rho>0$. For integers $N_L$ with $N_L/L^d\\to\\rho$, let $Z_{\\mathrm{per}}(L,N_L;\\beta)$ be the $1/N_L!$-normalized positional partition on the periodized cube, with the image convention of [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]. Then\n$$L^{-d}\\log Z_{\\mathrm{per}}(L,N_L;\\beta)\\longrightarrow F_\\beta(\\rho),$$\nthe same rate as the free cube. Let $C^{\\mathrm{per}}_{L,N_L}$ be the periodic exact-$N_L$ canonical law and $R_{L,\\omega}$ its periodized empirical field from [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]]. For any finite supporting activity $z>0$ of $F_\\beta$ at $\\rho$, these empirical fields concentrate in every open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood of the minimizer set of $I+\\beta\\Phi-\\rho\\log z$. A singleton minimizer gives convergence in probability in $\\tau_L$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "c61d43583847808018e118ae233c6b276cb20ee786fa7223e2d67df0188af4fd",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
