    "ex-tdmath-nonunique-variational-minimizers": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For stationary finite-intensity configuration laws, let $I(P)$ be relative entropy density with respect to the independent unit-intensity Poisson law, $\\rho(P)=E_PN_{[0,1)^d}$, and $\\Phi(P)$ the limiting positional energy density.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-specific-entropy-density",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "This is an information functional relative to the specified unit-intensity Poisson law; changing the reference changes its value.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-tdmath-relative-entropy-variational-and-chain-rules",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Then\n$$D(P_{XY}\\Vert Q_X\\otimes Q_Y)=D(P_X\\Vert Q_X)+\\int_X D(P_{Y|X=x}\\Vert Q_Y)\\,P_X(dx).$$\nMore generally, for nested standard-Borel observations $R$ and $S$ with $R$ a measurable function of $S$, and a fixed probability reference $Q_Y$ for a further variable $Y$, the conditional increments\n$$G(R):=E_P\\!\\left[D(P_{Y|R}\\Vert Q_Y)\\right],\\qquad G(S):=E_P\\!\\left[D(P_{Y|S}\\Vert Q_Y)\\right]$$\nsatisfy $0\\leq G(R)\\leq G(S)$ whenever the joint relative entropy is finite.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-tdmath-local-tame-topology",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Equivalently, a net $(P_\\alpha)$ converges to $P$ in $\\tau_L$ exactly when $E_{P_\\alpha}f\\to E_Pf$ for every measurable local $f$ with at most linear growth in the count of a bounded support.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "proof-step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $P,R$ be stationary laws of finite specific entropy and let $P_\\theta=\\theta P+(1-\\theta)R$. For a bounded cube $G$, the binary-label chain rule [F3] gives $$ \\theta D(P_G\\Vert Q_G)+(1-\\theta)D(R_G\\Vert Q_G) =D((P_\\theta)_G\\Vert Q_G)+I(S;X_G), $$ where $S$ is the mixture label and $X_G$ the observed configuration. Since $0\\leq I(S;X_G)\\leq H(S)<\\infty$, divide by $|G|$ and take the cube limit [F2]; $H(S)/|G|\\to0$, so $I(P_\\theta)=\\theta I(P)+(1-\\theta)I(R)$. The expectation defining $\\rho$ is affine. For finite energy densities, $E_{P_\\theta}H_G=\\theta E_PH_G+(1-\\theta)E_RH_G$ for every $G$; dividing by volume and taking limits gives affinity of $\\Phi$. Thus $J$ is affine on finite mixtures of finite-$J$ laws.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F3",
            "F2",
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "proof-step-2-1",
          "claim": "Applying step 1.1 to $P_0,P_1$ gives $J(P_\\theta)=\\theta J(P_0)+(1-\\theta)J(P_1)=m$, so every mixture is a minimizer. Put $P_{2n}=P_0$ and $P_{2n+1}=P_1$. The even and odd subsequences converge locally to $P_0$ and $P_1$. Since distinct laws differ on a bounded-region measurable event, its indicator is a bounded local test by [F4] with different expectations; the full sequence therefore has no $\\tau_L$ limit. Both accumulation points are minimizers.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F4",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "finite_checks": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Suppose $J(P)=I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z$ has two distinct stationary minimizers $P_0\\ne P_1$ with equal finite value $m$. Boundary empty: The Statement has no empty-configuration branch; its claim concerns the displayed positive-volume, density, or conditional regime.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Example",
            "source_excerpt": "Suppose $J(P)=I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z$ has two distinct stationary minimizers $P_0\\ne P_1$ with equal finite value $m$. Every finite mixture $P_\\theta=\\theta P_0+(1-\\theta)P_1$, $0\\leq\\theta\\leq1$, also minimizes $J$. The sequence of stationary laws alternating between $P_0$ and $P_1$ has two distinct local accumulation points and does not converge. This conditional mathematical example shows why compactness alone yields minimizer-set accumulation; it does not assert a finite-volume ensemble realizes the sequence or that a particular continuum potential exhibits coexistence.",
